                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1510-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sg.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Shotgun" title="Shotgun" ></span>Shure VP89S</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Shotgun Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The VP89S is a compact short shotgun microphone. It is the shortest mic of the modular VP89 series, which includes a single preamplifier body and three detachable capsule heads of varying lengths.</p><p>The VP89S kit includes the VP89 preamplifier body (aka the &#8220;RPM89/PRE&#8221;) and VP89S capsule head. The &#8216;S&#8217; in the model name stands for &#8216;Short.&#8217;</p><p>The VP89 head amplifier uses a transformer-coupled output circuit. The three capsule heads employ interference tubes made of aircraft-grade aluminum, nested within the aluminum exterior grille. The assembly is tested to survive a 12-foot drop without breaking. The capsules themselves are mounted at the rear of the interference tube, and are a half-inch electret design manufactured by Shure.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s frequency response has a natural taper below 200Hz, which is steeper with the onboard HPF filter engaged. It has a broad presence peak at 6kHz.</p><p>The 89S has a 70 degree acceptance angle, the widest of the three VP89 models, due to the shorter interference tube.</p><p>All VP89-series shotgun mics ship with a foam windscreen (Shure part number A89SW for the VP89S), and a cylindrical storage case (p/n A89SC for the VP89S).</p><p>The head amp, aka preamplifier, is available separately (p/n RPM89/PRE), as are the three &#8220;capsules&#8221;/interference tubes, as well as a unique &#8220;double-barrel&#8221; adapter that allows the head amplifier to be mounted alongside the interference tube to reduce the overall length of the unit (p/n A89U).</p><p>The VP89 mics are compatible with a variety of Rycote-manufactured windshields and Lyre mounts.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Shure/VP89S">Shure VP89S</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2011.</p>
